      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">How long does the car transport from Patna to Agra usually take?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">The typical transit time for Car Transport From Patna To Agra is 18‑22 hours, depending on traffic, weather, and any scheduled stops for safety checks. Our GPS‑enabled fleet provides real‑time updates, so you can monitor progress and anticipate the exact delivery window.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">What does the zero‑scratch guarantee cover during the Patna‑Agra move?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">Our zero‑scratch guarantee means the vehicle will be secured with hydraulic ramp loading, wheel chocks, and 7‑layer shock‑absorbent packaging. Any damage caused by our handling is fully covered by the IRDAI‑approved marine transit insurance, ensuring you receive your car exactly as it left Patna.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">Which documents are mandatory for interstate car transport between Patna and Agra?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">You must provide a valid registration certificate, original insurance policy, a GST‑compliant invoice, and an e‑Way bill generated for the shipment. A signed transport agreement is also required. Our team assists in preparing each document to avoid delays at state checkpoints.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">How is the price for Car Transport From Patna To Agra calculated?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">Pricing is based on the total distance (≈951 km), vehicle size, fuel surcharge, loading and unloading fees, insurance premium, and applicable GST. We offer a transparent cost sheet that itemises each charge, so you know exactly what you are paying for without hidden fees.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">Is insurance automatically included in the car transport service?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">Yes, every shipment includes 100 % declared‑value insurance approved by IRDAI. This covers accidental damage, theft, or loss during transit. You can also opt for additional coverage if you have a high‑value or classic vehicle, ensuring complete peace of mind.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">Can any type of car be shipped from Patna to Agra?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">We transport a wide range of vehicles, from compact cars and SUVs to luxury sedans and vintage models. Our multi‑axle hydraulic trailers have adjustable ramps and tie‑down points, allowing safe handling of both standard and oversized vehicles, provided they meet legal road‑worthiness.</p>
      </div>
